      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Location Sheet\n\nOne **location reference**: a clean, readable still of a place with no people, usable as an environment reference for storyboards and video.\n\n1. Rewrite the six boxes. Put the **place** first, then the **era and world rules**, then the objects that make it feel lived in.\n2. Run, then check **Save Image**.\n\nThe fixed negatives (no people, no modern objects, no text) are in **Build the location prompt**. If you change the era, change them too.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Location Sheet\n\nOne **location reference**: a clean, readable still of a place with no people, usable as an environment reference for storyboards and video.\n\n1. Rewrite the six boxes. Put the **place** first, then the **era and world rules**, then the objects that make it feel lived in.\n2. Run, then check **Save Image**.\n\nThe fixed negatives (no people, no modern objects, no text) are in **Build the location prompt**. If you change the era, change them too.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
